Subject: Propose changes as a pull request instead of naming write tools

Why: A change to a cluster or Google Cloud resource goes out as a pull request in the GitOps repository's format, never as a direct write; the gke MCP server offers read tools only (#2955) and the broker refuses kubectl and gcloud writes, so instructions naming write tools or write commands point the agent at paths it does not have and away from the pull request (#2935).
Local-Issue: #3185
Upstream-Issue: none (specific to this repository)
Retire-When: never; kube-agents proposes every change as a pull request

diff --git a/SKILL.md b/SKILL.md
--- a/SKILL.md
+++ b/SKILL.md
@@ -12,6 +12,8 @@ metadata:
 
 Guidance on configuring, optimizing, and troubleshooting GKE ComputeClasses.
 
+> A change goes out as a pull request to the GitOps repository, never as a write from here: Kubernetes objects as YAML through `gke-manifest-generation`, cluster settings and other Google Cloud resources as Config Connector YAML through `gcp-config-connector`, opened with `submit-suggestion`. Each profile's config offers only the `gke` MCP server's read tools, and the broker refuses `kubectl` and `gcloud` writes.
+
 ## When to Use
 
 -   **Cost optimization:** Spot VMs with on-demand fallback.
